{"type":"thinking","text":"I'm weighing how to keep the short separate inside this project, since the only entry is index.html at 1920x1080 and the editable parts are index.html and the section files under compositions/ and assets/. A standalone 1080x1920 composition file under compositions/ looks like the likeliest fit.

The "Chat" option is a new chat that starts from a copy of this one, which doesn't really give a separate project. The projects option only starts new videos when a message asks for several of them, so I'll check what the projects topic in the tool options says about starting a fresh project with a brief.

"}

{"type":"thinking","text":"I'm checking the project rules: a project needs at least two projects and only applies when several videos are requested, and the chat option says never for this kind of work. The person wants the short now, so I'll make it here as a separate composition inside this project. The open question is how it becomes its own video, since the render entry is index.html and replacing that would destroy the long film.

I'm weighing whether the short can render separately: the CLI may take a different entry or file argument, so I'm checking its help for options. A subfolder project would break the rule to edit only index.html, compositions/, and assets/, so a standalone composition file is the safer route.

"}

{"type":"thinking","text":"I'm checking whether a standalone composition file can skip the template wrapper when passed to `--composition`, since the caveat only covers template-wrapped sub-compositions. I'm leaning toward writing `compositions/short-rider-driver-pilot.html` as a full HTML document.

I'm weighing whether the check and snapshot commands accept a `--composition` option for a standalone file, since the caveat only mentions template wrappers. Checking their help output should settle it, since I can't confirm the app preview handles the file directly.

"}

{"type":"thinking","text":"I'm sorting out the caption placement for the portrait layout, which needs to sit roughly 600 to 700 px up from the bottom edge. That leaves little room for the content lanes above, so I'm weighing whether to move the captions lower or shrink the content area.

I'm working out the caption position and content lanes for the portrait frame. Moving the captions lower leaves a lot of empty space underneath, which I'll keep as a subtle glow and grid background, since the bottom area sits under the platform's UI overlay anyway.

